# Component Patterns

## Screen Routing

There is **no React Router** in this project. Do NOT install or use `react-router-dom` for
navigation. Screen transitions are managed by `useAppLoader` phases in `src/App.tsx`:

```
startup → pairing → loading → ready
   ↓          ↓                  ↓
LoadingScreen  PairingScreen   DisplayScreen
```

The `AppRoutes` component in `App.tsx` determines which screen to render based on the
current phase. Transitions use crossfade animations (700ms) with a minimum loading
time of 3500ms to prevent flicker.

```typescript
const targetScreen = useMemo((): ScreenType => {
  if (phase === 'pairing' && hasPairingCode) return 'pairing';
  if (phase === 'ready') return 'display';
  return 'loading';
}, [phase, hasPairingCode]);
```

## Lazy Loading

All screen-level components are loaded with `React.lazy()`:

```typescript
const LoadingScreen = lazy(() => import('./components/screens/LoadingScreen'));
const PairingScreen = lazy(() => import('./components/screens/PairingScreen'));
const DisplayScreen = lazy(() => import('./components/screens/DisplayScreen'));
```

Wrapped in `<Suspense fallback={null}>` — the loading overlay handles visual feedback
during the initial load, so Suspense fallback is intentionally null.

## Component Hierarchy

```
src/components/
├── screens/           Top-level phase components (one per app phase)
│   ├── LoadingScreen    Progress bar, task list, logo animation
│   ├── PairingScreen    QR code display for pairing
│   └── DisplayScreen    Main display — delegates to layout components
├── layout/            Orientation-aware wrappers
│   ├── OrientationWrapper   Detects physical vs desired orientation, applies CSS rotation
│   ├── LandscapeLayout      Landscape-specific grid layout
│   └── PortraitLayout       Portrait-specific stacked layout
└── display/           Reusable display components
    ├── Header             Masjid name, date, connection status
    ├── Footer             Branding, version info
    ├── PrayerTimesPanel   Prayer times grid with active/next highlighting
    ├── PrayerCountdown    Countdown timer to next prayer
    ├── ContentCarousel    Rotating announcements/events/Islamic content
    └── IslamicPattern     Background decorative SVG pattern
```

**Rules**:
- `screens/` components handle top-level data fetching and phase logic
- `layout/` components handle orientation and spatial arrangement only
- `display/` components are reusable and receive data via props or selectors
- Barrel exports in `index.ts` files for `layout/` and `display/`

## Orientation Handling

The app supports both landscape and portrait orientations. The desired orientation comes
from the backend (`screenContent.screen.orientation`). If the physical display orientation
does not match the desired one, `OrientationWrapper` applies a CSS 90-degree rotation:

```typescript
const { shouldRotate } = useRotationHandling(orientation);

// When shouldRotate is true, the layout is rendered inside a container with:
// transform: translate(-50%, -50%) rotate(90deg)
// width: 100vh / height: 100vw (swapped dimensions)
```

This is a CSS-only rotation — no Electron or OS-level rotation is used.

## Component Structure Order

Every component should follow this ordering:

```typescript
/**
 * ComponentName
 *
 * Brief description of what this component renders and why.
 */
const ComponentName: React.FC<Props> = ({ prop1, prop2 }) => {
  // 1. Redux hooks
  const dispatch = useAppDispatch();
  const data = useAppSelector(selectData);

  // 2. Refs (for preventing re-renders, tracking previous values)
  const previousValueRef = useRef<string | null>(null);

  // 3. Local state
  const [isVisible, setIsVisible] = useState(false);

  // 4. Effects (with cleanup)
  useEffect(() => {
    const interval = setInterval(tick, 1000);
    return () => clearInterval(interval);
  }, []);

  // 5. Memoised callbacks
  const handleEvent = useCallback(() => {
    dispatch(someAction());
  }, [dispatch]);

  // 6. Render helpers (for complex sub-sections)
  const renderHeader = () => <div>...</div>;

  // 7. Loading / error guards (early returns)
  if (isLoading) return <div className="animate-shimmer" />;
  if (error) return <div className="text-alert-red">{error}</div>;
  if (!data) return null;

  // 8. Main render
  return (
    <div className="panel">
      {renderHeader()}
      {/* ... */}
    </div>
  );
};

export default ComponentName;
```

**Rules**:
- All components use `default export`
- JSDoc comment on every component explaining its purpose
- Always check loading/error/null states before rendering data
- Use `useAppDispatch` and `useAppSelector` (typed hooks), not `useDispatch`/`useSelector`

## Error Boundary

`App.tsx` wraps the entire app in `<ErrorBoundary>` from `react-error-boundary`:

- Displays an error message with a "Reload" button
- Calls `window.location.reload()` on reset (auto-recovery for kiosk mode)
- Logs errors via `logger.error()`

Do NOT add additional error boundaries unless isolating a specific failure domain
(e.g., a single carousel slide that should not crash the entire display).

## Emergency Overlay

The `EmergencyOverlay` in `App.tsx` renders a full-screen alert when `emergencySlice.currentAlert`
is non-null:

- Colour schemes: red, orange, amber, blue, green, purple, dark
- Fade-in/fade-out animation with mount/unmount lifecycle
- Auto-clears when `expiresAt` passes
- Respects orientation rotation
- Z-index 9999 — always on top of everything

## Screen Transition System

Transitions between screens use a controlled animation system:

| Constant | Value | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `TRANSITION_MS` | 700ms | Crossfade duration |
| `MIN_LOADING_MS` | 3500ms | Minimum time on loading screen (prevents flicker) |
| `POST_READY_DELAY` | 400ms | Delay after ready before transitioning |

The loading screen is an overlay that fades out to reveal the content screen underneath.
This prevents a blank flash during lazy-loading.

## Custom Hooks Usage

Do NOT reimplement logic that exists in these hooks:

| Hook | Returns | Use for |
|---|---|---|
| `useAppLoader` | `phase`, `overallProgress`, `currentTask`, `tasks`, `hasPairingCode` | App lifecycle |
| `usePrayerTimes` | Prayer times, current/next prayer, countdown, Hijri date | Prayer display |
| `useCurrentTime` | Reactive `Date` object, updates every second | Clock display |
| `useConnectionStatus` | Online/offline state, WebSocket status | Status indicators |
| `useRotationHandling` | `shouldRotate`, rotation styles | Orientation |
| `useDevKeyboard` | (void — registers keyboard listeners) | Dev shortcuts |

```typescript
// CORRECT: Use the existing hook
import usePrayerTimes from '@/hooks/usePrayerTimes';
const { prayerTimes, nextPrayer, countdown } = usePrayerTimes();

// WRONG: Reimplement prayer time logic
const nextPrayer = useMemo(() => {
  // 50 lines of calculation that already exists in usePrayerTimes
}, []);
```

## Do NOT

- Install or use React Router — routing is phase-based in `App.tsx`
- Add `onClick` handlers or interactive elements (this is a display-only app)
- Add additional error boundaries without justification
- Use untyped `useDispatch`/`useSelector` — use the typed variants from `src/store/hooks.ts`
- Create components without JSDoc comments
- Skip loading/error/null guards before rendering data
- Add user-facing scrollbars, text inputs, or form elements
